For https://github.com/OpenEnroth/OpenEnroth/pull/1984

Trace sells or tries to sell three different recipes (first, water resistance, last), a spellbook and a message scroll to the magic shop on Emerald Isle. Positive result will have sold only the spell book, without the fix the recipes will be sold too.

As yet un-pushed test code:

Subject: [PATCH] Game test for recipes no longer sellable in magic shops
---
Index: test/Bin/GameTest/GameTests_1500.cpp
<+>UTF-8
===================================================================
diff --git a/test/Bin/GameTest/GameTests_1500.cpp b/test/Bin/GameTest/GameTests_1500.cpp
--- a/test/Bin/GameTest/GameTests_1500.cpp	(revision 9ad07e3650013e64704b30499009078ec5685601)
+++ b/test/Bin/GameTest/GameTests_1500.cpp	(revision 9ffec7e9e92528dc89a28467cb983a7d3738e8db)
@@ -682,3 +682,18 @@
     EXPECT_GT(pSpriteObjects[4].containing_item.numCharges, 0);
     EXPECT_GT(pSpriteObjects[4].containing_item.maxCharges, 0);
 }
+
+GAME_TEST(Issues, Issue1983) {
+    // It was possible to sell recipes at a magic shop, not only at the alchemist as intended.
+    auto recipeTape = tapes.hasItem(ITEM_RECIPE_REJUVENATION);
+    auto bookTape = tapes.hasItem(ITEM_SPELLBOOK_LIGHT_BOLT);
+    auto letterTape = tapes.hasItem(ITEM_MESSAGE_LETTER_FROM_MR_STANTLEY_2);
+    auto houseTape = tapes.house();
+    auto goldTape = tapes.gold();
+    test.playTraceFromTestData("issue_1983.mm7", "issue_1983.json");
+    EXPECT_EQ(recipeTape, tape(true)); // The recipe should still be there
+    EXPECT_EQ(bookTape, tape(true, false)); // The spellbook should be gone
+    EXPECT_EQ(letterTape, tape(true)); // The letter should still be there
+    EXPECT_CONTAINS(houseTape, HOUSE_MAGIC_SHOP_EMERALD_ISLAND);
+    EXPECT_EQ(goldTape.delta(), 365); // Sold the spellbook
+}

... maybe a bit too much, but I wanted to see these working (also tried a few intentional deviations or comparing the gold tape to a tuple to get a feel. Nice framework).

Anyway, that need not be the final test code, but I have convinced myself that the trace allows one that can distinguish fixed/unfixed.
